  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "James",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 3,
    "summary": "By governing the tongue, we gain perfection—Heavenly wisdom is pure, peaceable, and full of mercy.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "My brethren, be not many masters, knowing that we shall receive the greater condemnation.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "JST James 3:1 … strive not for the mastery, knowing that in so doing we shall receive the greater condemnation."
          },
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 32,
            "text": "GR (also) teachers."
          },
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 63,
            "text": "D&C 82:3."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For in many things we offend all. If any man offend not in word, the same is a perfect man, and able also to bridle the whole body.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 32,
            "text": "GR stumble, err."
          },
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 55,
            "text": "TG Offense."
          },
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 63,
            "text": "Ps. 39:1; Prov. 21:23."
          },
          {
            "start": 79,
            "end": 86,
            "text": "TG Perfection."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 74,
            "end": 76
          },
          {
            "start": 92,
            "end": 95
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold, we put bits in the horses’ mouths, that they may obey us; and we turn about their whole body.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold also the ships, which though they be so great, and are driven of fierce winds, yet are they turned about with a very small helm, whithersoever the governor listeth.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 154,
            "end": 162,
            "text": "GR helmsman, pilot."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 43
          },
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 61
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Even so the tongue is a little member, and boasteth great things. Behold, how great a matter a little fire kindleth!",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 51,
            "text": "TG Boast; Rashness."
          },
          {
            "start": 86,
            "end": 92,
            "text": "GR forest."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And the tongue is a fire, a world of iniquity: so is the tongue among our members, that it defileth the whole body, and setteth on fire the course of nature; and it is set on fire of hell.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 14,
            "text": "Prov. 16:27; Mark 7:20 (19–23); Alma 12:14; D&C 88:121."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 17
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For every kind of beasts, and of birds, and of serpents, and of things in the sea, is tamed, and hath been tamed of mankind:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But the tongue can no man tame; it is an unruly evil, full of deadly poison.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 14,
            "text": "TG Gossip; Profanity."
          },
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 47,
            "text": "GR untameable, uncontrollable."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 37
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Therewith bless we God, even the Father; and therewith curse we men, which are made after the similitude of God.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 60,
            "text": "TG Curse."
          },
          {
            "start": 94,
            "end": 104,
            "text": "TG God, Body of, Corporeal Nature."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Out of the same mouth proceedeth blessing and cursing. My brethren, these things ought not so to be.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 21,
            "text": "Matt. 12:34; Luke 6:45. TG Hypocrisy."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Doth a fountain send forth at the same place sweet water and bitter?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "GR spring, well. Moro. 7:11 (6–11)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 56
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Can the fig tree, my brethren, bear olive berries? either a vine, figs? so can no fountain both yield salt water and fresh.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 75,
            "end": 78
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Who is a wise man and endued with knowledge among you? let him shew out of a good conversation his works with meekness of wisdom.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 82,
            "end": 94,
            "text": "Prov. 12:13 (13–19)."
          },
          {
            "start": 110,
            "end": 118,
            "text": "TG Meek."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 6
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But if ye have bitter envying and strife in your hearts, glory not, and lie not against the truth.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "TG Strife."
          },
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 66,
            "text": "GR do not assume superiority over."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "This wisdom descendeth not from above, but is earthly, sensual, devilish.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 45
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For where envying and strife is, there is confusion and every evil work.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 17,
            "text": "TG Envy."
          },
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 28,
            "text": "TG Contention."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 32
          },
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 41
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But the wisdom that is from above is first pure, then peaceable, gentle, and easy to be entreated, full of mercy and good fruits, without partiality, and without hypocrisy.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 14,
            "text": "TG God, Intelligence of; Wisdom."
          },
          {
            "start": 77,
            "end": 97,
            "text": "GR pliant, easily persuaded."
          },
          {
            "start": 107,
            "end": 112,
            "text": "TG God, Mercy of."
          },
          {
            "start": 162,
            "end": 171,
            "text": "D&C 121:42."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 73,
            "end": 76
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And the fruit of righteousness is sown in peace of them that make peace.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 30,
            "text": "TG Righteousness."
          },
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 47,
            "text": "TG Peace; Peace of God."
          },
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 71,
            "text": "TG Peacemakers."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
